  greetings:
  - Mind the dog. We don't have a dog. Mind it anyway.
  - Detective. Silas said you'd come round.
  aboutSelf: Married Silas when I was nineteen. Raised two boys and lost a hand. Got a hook for it. I don't miss the hand.
  aboutTown: Semblance doesn't like change. We're all a bit broken, and we're used to the shape of each other's broken bits.
  seenAnythingStrange: Something's been taking eggs out from under the hens without waking them. Shells left whole, a neat hole in one end. Sucked dry.
  foundersDay: Rained. Mae won with her cherry, Greta came second with her apple, and the Father talked about weeds. Same as every year.
  gossip:
  - title: About Irene Vance
    response: Irene's right eye sits up high. Gives her a look like she's always asking a question.
  - title: About Greta Kessler
    response: Greta's right ear sits up high. Hats never sit straight on her.
